# File structure

## Components — folder + index.tsx only

- Each component lives in its own PascalCase folder; implementation is `index.tsx`.
- Next to it when needed: `types.ts`, `styles.module.css`, `hooks/`, `components/` (nested).
- Never create a component as a lone `.ts` / `.tsx` file in the parent folder.
- UI primitives: `src/ui/Button/` (PascalCase). Feature namespaces may use lowercase folders (`features/header/`).
- Page-only sections live under `src/pages/PageName/` (e.g. `pages/Home/HeroSection`), not `src/components/`.

```
src/components/CroppedText/
  index.tsx
  types.ts
  styles.module.css
```

## Split by content type

- Constants → `consts.ts` (or `consts/`) inside the feature. No magic lists or URLs in `index.tsx`.
- Routes → `src/routes/paths.ts`. Do not hardcode `'/catalog'` (or similar) in components.
- Types → local `types.ts` if used only here; shared types in `src/types/`.
- Utilities → `utils/`. Hooks → `hooks/`.
- Do not mix: no constants in component files, no types inside utils.

## Component props — OwnProps → Props

- Define local `OwnProps` in `types.ts`; export `Props = FC<OwnProps>`.
- Component: `export const Foo: Props = (...) => { ... }`.
- Do not export `OwnProps`. Do not type as `React.FC<...>` inline in `index.tsx`.

```ts
import type { FC } from 'react'

type OwnProps = {
  text: string | undefined
  length?: number
}

export type Props = FC<OwnProps>
```

## Exports and imports

- Named exports for components (`export const Foo`). Not `export default`.
- Exceptions: `App.tsx`, `src/i18n/index.ts`, Vite config.
- Relative imports inside `src/` (e.g. `../../ui/Button`). Do not use the `@/` alias in new or touched code.
- No barrel `index.ts` whose only job is re-exporting siblings. Import the concrete file.

## Extensions

- React components — always `.tsx`. Pure TS — `.ts`. Styles — `styles.module.css`.
